The proposed var09 classification must rehash the accepted parent report, closure, original raw files, evidence index, and frozen independent postrun GO that already records the complete 4,044-cell report acceptance. A new classification reader may make small, predeclared report projection assertions relevant to the ID0 chain, but must keep those assertions separate from the prior full-report verdict. It must not invoke the accepted checker again or claim a fresh independent 4,044-cell acceptance for var09. The full 118-line/104-timed-event original log and source row remain the direct evidence for the narrow after-transfer task chain.

All other feasibility limits stand: one accepted parent run is reused; no new native run or checker invocation is authorized; no second or reverse transfer, general priority rule, hidden person identity, or whole-var09 claim follows. A separate prospective classification contract and independent review are still required before a new package or catalog entry.
